676|   - crandc BA read mask &0x8000001 (1|1<<27): `ba & !bb' is a bitwise AND with !bb in {0,1}: only bit 0 of ba (= CR[BA]) can reach the condition
677|   - crandc BA read mask &0x10000001 (1|1<<28): `ba & !bb' is a bitwise AND with !bb in {0,1}: only bit 0 of ba (= CR[BA]) can reach the condition
678|   - crandc BA read mask &0x20000001 (1|1<<29): `ba & !bb' is a bitwise AND with !bb in {0,1}: only bit 0 of ba (= CR[BA]) can reach the condition
679|   - crandc BA read mask &0x40000001 (1|1<<30): `ba & !bb' is a bitwise AND with !bb in {0,1}: only bit 0 of ba (= CR[BA]) can reach the condition
680|   - crandc BA read mask &0x80000001 (1|1<<31): `ba & !bb' is a bitwise AND with !bb in {0,1}: only bit 0 of ba (= CR[BA]) can reach the condition
681|   - crandc read statements swapped: the two reads are independent of each other and of the clear (which follows both)
682|   - crorc read statements swapped: the two reads are independent of each other and of the clear (which follows both)
683| 
684| EXCLUDED / DISCLOSED (1 cell):
685|   - crandc clear -> toggle (^=): disclosed in the probe's clause (e)(5): every crandc row with result 0 pre-sets the inverse
686| 
687| STILL UNDETECTED BY THE 70 ROWS (0 cells):
688| 
689| ## THE 4 ROUND-3 ROWS (single-instruction sessions shaped like the `hi'/pin rows; each compares the WHOLE CR, from the
690| register dump and from mfcr r10, with the architectural CR)
691| 
692|   64 crorc baread   crorc BT=17 BA=31 BB=5 seed=0xfffffffe want CR=0xffffbffe  CR[BT] pre-set inverse (1)
693|   64 crorc bbread   crorc BT=30 BA=30 BB=31 seed=0xfffffffc want CR=0xfffffffe  CR[BT] pre-set inverse (0) = the BA source
694|   64 crandc setbits crandc BT=31 BA=30 BB=31 seed=0x00000002 want CR=0x00000003  CR[BT] pre-set inverse (0)
695|   64 crorc setbits  crorc BT=31 BA=0 BB=31 seed=0x00000000 want CR=0x00000001  CR[BT] pre-set inverse (0) = the BB source
696| 
697|   64 crorc baread   crorc 17,31,5 over 0xfffffffe: a = CR[31] = 0, b = CR[5] = 1 -> 0.  The BA read shifts by 0, so a = CR & m: every
698|                     mask m with ANY bit 1..31 set reads nonzero and gives 1 (codex B2's & 0x8001 reads CR[16] = 1 here; the
699|                     round-2 `64 crorc bamask' row has CR[16] = 0, its destination).  Also: every BA field mask 0..30 (CR[m] = 1),
700|                     mask 16 included, which repairs R1.
701|   64 crorc bbread   crorc 30,30,31 over 0xfffffffc: a = CR[30] = 0, b = CR[31] = 0 -> 1 at CR[30] (its own pre-set inverse 0 IS
702|                     the a = 0 source).  The BB read shifts by 0: every mask m with any bit 2..31 set reads nonzero, !bb = 0, 0
703|                     (B1, k = 2..31); bit 1 = CR[30] = 0 here, and `& 3' / `& 7' are red on `64 crorc 00' (its BB = 2 read is 2).
704|   64 crandc setbits crandc 31,30,31 over 0x00000002: a = CR[30] = 1, b = CR[31] = 0 -> 1 at CR[31]; the set shifts by 0, so a
705|                     literal 1+2^k also sets CR[31-k]: zero in the seed for k = 2..31 (B3 and k = 31); k = 1 lands on CR[30] = 1,
706|                     the source, and is red on `64 crandc 01' (crandc 10,1,0 sets CR[9] after `crandc 9' cleared it).
707|   64 crorc setbits  crorc 31,0,31 over 0: a = b = 0 -> 1 at CR[31]; every extra bit CR[31-k], k = 1..31, lands on a zero (B4).
708| 
709| WHY FOUR AND NO FEWER (single-instruction sessions).  The four open families need, respectively: (i) crorc with a = 0, b = 1,
710| result 0 and CR[16] = 1 (B2); (ii) crorc with a = 0, b = 0 (result 1) and CR[0..29] all 1 so that a BB read shifted by 0 has
711| bits 2..31 set (B1); (iii) crandc with result 1 and zeros at CR[BT-k] for k = 7, 9, 11..31 (B3); (iv) crorc with result 1 and
712| zeros at CR[BT-26], CR[BT-27] (B4).  (i) and (ii)/(iv) differ in the result; (ii) needs ones where (iv) needs zeros (the
713| extra set bits of (iv) at BT-26, BT-27 lie in 0..5 for any BT, inside (ii)'s ones at 0..29, and moving BT below 27 shifts
714| (iv)'s bits out); (iii) is crandc.  So no single instruction serves two families, and 4 rows is the minimum; a multi-
715| instruction session would cost more rows (session/others/mfcr/disasm), as the edge session shows.  (The round-2 rows are
716| kept as measured: they were not the minimum, see r2_20261105/CLOSURE.errata.md.)
717| 
718| ## PROOF: the whole 2^32 constant space at the six sites (what the contract may claim beyond the enumerated cells)
719| 
720| A read is a = (cr >> (31-x)) & m with x the field index; call q = cr >> (31-x), whose bit j is CR[x-j] (j <= x, zero above).
721|   crandc BA (:2732):  the condition `ba & !bb' is bitwise with !bb in {0,1}, so only bit 0 of a counts.  m with bit 0 set:
722|                       EQUIVALENT (32 of them enumerated here).  m with bit 0 clear: a & 1 = 0, the result is always 0, red on
723|                       `64 crandc 10' (want 1).  Closed for every m.
724|   crandc BB (:2733):  `!bb' sees only bb != 0.  `64 crandc bbmask' (BB = 31, q = 0xfffffffe, want 1 needs bb = 0): any m with a
725|                       bit in 1..31 reads nonzero -> red.  m = 0: bb = 0 always, crandc becomes CR[BA], red on `64 crandc 11'.
726|                       Closed for every m != 1.
727|   crorc BA (:2759):   `ba | !bb' sees only a != 0.  `64 crorc baread' (BA = 31, q = 0xfffffffe, want 0 needs a = 0): any m with
728|                       a bit in 1..31 -> red.  m = 0: a = 0 always, crorc becomes !CR[BB], red on `64 crorc 11'.  Closed.
729|   crorc BB (:2760):   `64 crorc bbread' (BB = 31, q = 0xfffffffc, want 1 needs bb = 0): any m with a bit in 2..31 -> red; m
730|                       with bit 1: `64 crorc 00' (q = 2, want 1) -> red; m = 0: bb = 0 always, result always 1, red on
731|                       `64 crorc 01'.  Closed.
732|   set literal C (:2736, :2763): cr |= (C << (31-BT)).  C without bit 0: CR[BT] is never set, red on every result-1 row.  C with
733|                       bit 0 and some other bit j: on the `setbits' rows (BT = 31) the extra bit lands on CR[31-j], a zero for
734|                       j = 2..31 (crandc) and j = 1..31 (crorc), seen by the whole-CR compare; j = 1 at crandc is red on
735|                       `64 crandc 01'.  Closed for every C != 1 (and C = 0 is `set deleted').
736|   The field masks `& 31' (:2730-2731, :2757-2758) are closed over 0..30 by enumeration; a mask with bits above 4 is the fix
737|   (the field is 5 bits), so the mask sites are closed over every constant too.
738| 
739| ## WHAT STAYS UNDETECTED, AND WHY
740| 
741|   - the 36 EQUIVALENT cells above (proved; no row can see them);
742|   - crandc clear -> toggle (^=): DISCLOSED in the probe's clause (e)(5) (every crandc row with result 0 pre-sets the inverse,
743|     and the round-3 `64 crandc setbits' row pre-sets 0 with result 1: a toggle of 0 then |= gives 1 too);
744|   - OUTSIDE the denominator (disclosed, (e)(5)): an extra CLEAR (clear literal 1+2^k).  The round-3 whole-CR rows see some of
745|     them incidentally (appendix); the rest need ones at non-source, non-destination bits, which the set-literal rows cannot
746|     carry.  Not claimed.
747| 
748| ## PROBE CONTRACT TEXT (clause (e), round 3)
749| 
750|   ROUND 3 (regress/artifacts/ppccrandcorc/r3_20261105/CLOSURE3.md): the four whole-CR rows after the round-2 pins close the
751|   single-constant space at the four read-mask sites and the two set literals.  COVERED: every read mask `& m' other than the
752|   fix's at crandc BB, crorc BA and crorc BB (all 2^32 m, by the proof; 1+2^k for k = 1..31 and 0, 2, 4, 6 enumerated and
753|   simulated), every crandc BA read mask with bit 0 clear; every set literal C != 1 in both handlers (1+2^k, k = 1..31,
754|   enumerated); the clear/set addressing cells (31-bt) -> (31-ba), (31-bb), bt and the clear moved between the reads.
755|   DELIBERATELY UNCOVERED: crandc BA read masks with bit 0 set (EQUIVALENT: `ba & !bb' sees only bit 0 of ba); `|=' -> `^='
756|   at either set (EQUIVALENT after the clear); the read statements swapped (EQUIVALENT); the crandc toggle of (5); an extra
757|   CLEAR of a non-source, non-destination bit (5).
